-- RUNG 23 SCALING CONFIG: the config that does NOT fit one-shot under a fixed RSS cap.
--
-- The transparency oracle (r23_segmented_train.rail) runs d=8/hidden=64/ctx=8/epochs=19 and proves
-- segmented head == one-shot head bit-for-bit -- but that config FITS one-shot, so it cannot by
-- itself substantiate the scaling claim. This file is the scaling half: it scales the ONE axis the
-- proven architecture admits WITHOUT a bit-exactness-breaking rewrite -- hidden (the readout MLP
-- width, fully dimension-generic via gpu_matvec / lm4_matvec_t) -- to hidden=256 (the gate's
-- "hidden>=256" alternative), and scales epochs + corpus so the transient training garbage + canon
-- string size of a ONE-SHOT run exceed a fixed per-process RSS cap, while the SEGMENTED run (a
-- bnd_wp_ser -> arena_reset -> bnd_wp_deser per segment) stays under it.
--
-- WHY NOT d>=32 / ctx>=32: the proven RoPE is hardcoded to d=8/ctx=8 -- rope_row reads exactly 8
-- slots and the cos/sin tables are exactly 32 entries (8 positions x 4 pairs). Scaling d or ctx
-- requires a GENERALIZED variable-d RoPE that does not exist in the lineage; building one bit-exact
-- is a separate prerequisite (out of this rung's scope, and risky under compute discipline). hidden
-- is the honest, bit-exact-safe scaling axis. This is stated, not hidden, per the rung's own ethos.
--
-- This config is SEGMENTED-ONLY: there is no one-shot oracle here, because by construction the
-- one-shot run is the thing that does not fit. The transparency equality is proven on the oracle
-- config; this config proves the segmentation ENABLES a run a one-shot cap would kill. The
-- per-segment peak RSS is measured by rail_trace in validate.sh; the scaling claim is:
--   peak RSS(segmented) << peak RSS(one-shot would need)   [one-shot OOM/cap-kill is the witness].
--
-- Build: ./rail_native --out-prefix rungs/r23/out/r23s_bin rungs/r23/r23_scaled_train.rail
-- Run (UNDER A CAP): RAIL_ARENA_MB=8192 ./rungs/r23/out/r23s_bin
-- Trace peak RSS:    ./rail_native run tools/trace/rail_trace.rail rungs/r23/r23_scaled_train.rail
--
-- It shares the proven lm10 transformer + bnd round-trip + segment driver. To avoid duplicating
-- ~600 lines, the orchestrator builds this by `import`-style reuse: see IMPL.md "How to build the
-- scaled config" -- the BODY is identical to r23_segmented_train.rail except main's dims. The
-- canonical, self-contained source is generated by validate.sh from the oracle file with a dims
-- patch (sed), keeping ONE source of truth for the ~600 lines of proven machinery.
--
-- The dims this config sets (the only delta from the oracle's main):
--   hidden  = 256   (gate: hidden>=256; bit-exact-safe, readout MLP is dimension-generic)
--   epochs  = 120   (more transient garbage + larger canon body -> one-shot RSS pressure)
--   corpus  = tools/bitexact/lm10_corpus_big.txt  (more pairs -> per-epoch garbage scales)
--   seg_epochs = 20 (=> nsegs = ceil(120/20) = 6 >= 4 segments)
--
-- See r23_scaled_dims.txt for the exact patch the orchestrator applies.
0
